            <ArticleTitle>Nematode infection mimicking paratesticular malignancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-200775</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013200775</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paratesticular swellings pose a diagnostic dilemma due to concerns over malignancy. We present a case of paratesticular swelling in a 13-year-old boy as a result of Dirofilaria immitis infection. The boy presented with a 2-month history of right testicular discomfort associated with an irregular mass within the scrotum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
